[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:SOS]
[00:13.19]How did the woman get help?
[00:18.14]When a light passenger plane flew off course some time ago,
[00:23.05]it crashed in the mountains and its pilot was killed.
[00:28.04]The only passengers, a young woman and her two baby daughters, were unhurt.
[00:36.59]It was the middle of winter.
[00:38.87]Snow lay thick on the ground.
[00:42.74]The woman knew that the nearest village was miles away.
[00:48.02]When it grew dark, she turned a suitcase into a bed and put the children inside it,
[00:56.46]covering them with all the clothes she could find.
[01:00.84]During the night, it got terribly cold.
[01:05.64]The woman kept as near as she could to the children
[01:09.52]and even tried to get into the case herself, but it was too small.
[01:16.30]Early next morning,
[01:18.11]she heard planes passing overhead and wondered how she could send a signal.
[01:25.27]Then she had an idea She stamped out the letters 'SOS' in the snow.
[01:34.85]Fortunately, a pilot saw the signal and sent a message by radio to the nearest town.
[01:42.89]It was not long before a helicopter arrived on the scene to rescue the survivors of the plane crash.
